`Shipment` is a mutable struct with public fields `int Weight` and `List<string> Labels`.

```csharp
var original = new Shipment
{
    Weight = 12,
    Labels = new List<string> { "fragile" }
};
var copy = original;
copy.Weight = 20;
copy.Labels.Add("urgent");
copy.Labels = new List<string> { "returned" };
```

Explain what `copy = original` copies and why changing `Weight`, adding a label, and replacing `Labels` affect `original` differently. Include the final contents of `original`.

`Meter` is a class with a public `int Reading` field.

```csharp
var first = new Meter { Reading = 8 };
var second = first;
second.Reading = 15;
second = new Meter { Reading = 30 };
```

A student says: “Because `Reading` is an integer, changing it through `second` cannot affect `first`.” Explain the mistake and why the final assignment to `second` has a different effect. Include the final reading reachable through each variable.
